*9/18/86 Rework handling of local vs. net origin of mail.        [1.24]
*[1.20] 2/12/85 - try to prevent net mailer-mailer loops!
*       Replace "AT" with "@".  Remove blanks from "From:" line.
*[1.11] - Fix grammar in EMSG1.
*[1] X1.9 - REPLACE =V(ARPADATE) WITH REFERENCE TO MAILBLOK POINTER.
*
MAILRET  TITLE 'CUCCA VM NETWORK MAILER VERSION 1 - RETURN TO SENDER'
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*      MAILER -- Copyright (c) 1982,1986 Columbia University.         *
*    Program Property of the Trustees of Columbia University in the   *
*    City of New York.                                                *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
MAILRET  CSECT ,
* MAILRET -
* Mailret is called when an error has occurred in processing a
* mail file that has resulted in one, some, or all of the designated
* message recipients not to receive a copy of the file.  Such errors
* as a non-existent user or host name, invalid syntax or other
* qualifications decided by the user validation exits and/or VALIDATE
* determine if a file is to be returned.  The file is returned as
* the body of a new message that this routine generates that
* contains an explanation of the errors.  The file is returned to
* it's sender differently based on these tests:                  [1.24]
*  1) If the (from/sender) MAILSFLD is valid,  send return mail  [1.24]
*     to that address after checking case (3) below.             [1.24]
*  2) If MAILSFLD is invalid,  send return mail to the spool file[1.24]
*     origin: MAILUSER@MAILNODE after checking case (3) below.   [1.24]
*  3) EXCEPT when sender (MAILSFLD or MAILUSER@MAILNODE) is      [1.24]
*     listed as a mail server (in one of the tables) in          [1.24]
*     which case,  bounce the mail to local postmaster since a   [1.24]
*     trusted mail server should never generate an invalid sender[1.24]
*     field (ha!).  This aids preventing mail loops.             [1.24]
*  In both cases, the return file is punched to this machine's
*  reader to allow the usual processing of mail files.  Looping
*  may develop if the file generated here has an error, so it
*  is the responsibilty of this machine to check for files
*  destined to itself and process them specially (i.e. send them
*  to the maintainer userid or throw them away).
*  To aid VALIDATE in determining whether a file punched to *    [1.24]
*  is an error reply or something that RSCS rejected and         [1.24]
*  transferred back, the tag is set to "--- returned mail file ---".
*  The tag on files returned by RSCS will be "<nodename> <userid>".
*
*
*  CALLED VIA -
*    CALL MAILRET,(MAILBLOK)
PAB      DSECT ,
@MBLOK   DS    A             ADDRESS OF MAILBLOK
         SPACE ,
*
         SPACE
* REGISTER USAGE -
R0  EQU  0 -
R1  EQU  1 -
R2  EQU  2 -
R3  EQU  3 -
R4  EQU  4 -
R5  EQU  5 -
R6  EQU  6 -
R7  EQU  7 -
R8  EQU  8 -
R9  EQU  9 -
R10 EQU 10 -
R11 EQU 11 - MAILBLOK BASE
R12 EQU 12 - PROGRAM BASE
R13 EQU 13 - SAVE AREA
R14 EQU 14 - SUBROUTINE LINKAGE
R15 EQU 15 - SUBROUTINE LINKAGE
         SPACE
         AIF   ('&SYSPARM' NE 'SUP').NOSUP                       [1.23]
         PRINT NOGEN
.NOSUP   ANOP  ,                                                 [1.23]
         BLOCKS
         MAILBLOK
         EJECT
MAILRET  CSECT ,
         USING MAILRET,R15   TEMPORARY ADDRESSABILITY
         B     EYESKIP       BRANCH OVER EYESKIP
MYNAME   DC    CL8'MAILRET',CL8'&SYSDATE'
EYESKIP  DS    0H
         DROP  R15
         STM   R14,R12,12(R13) SAVE CALLER'S REGS
         LR    R12,R15       PERMANENT ADDRESSABILITY
         USING MAILRET,R12
         LA    R14,SAVE      MY SAVE AREA
         ST    R13,4(R14)    SAVE CALLER'S PTR
         ST    R14,8(R13)    CHAIN MINE BACK
         LR    R13,R14       SET MY SAVE PTR
         USING PAB,R1        ADDRESS PLIST
         L     R11,@MBLOK    GET MAILBLOK BASE
         USING MAILBLOK,R11  ADDRESS IT
         DROP  R1            DONE WITH PLIST
         SPACE ,
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
* (1) Check validity of sender field (MAILSFLD)                  [1.24]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
* MAILSFLD may in fact be syntactically valid even though not    [1.24]
* semantically.  That is, VALIDATE found the sender/from to be   [1.24]
* a counterfeit.  VALIDATE will also notice a RCSC rejection,    [1.24]
* so first check for that before general case of VALIDATE fail.  [1.24]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
         XC    MBOXP,MBOXP         Clear MBOX pointer.
         TM    MAILFLG1,MFLG1REJ RSCS reject the file?           [1.24]
         BO    RSCSREJ       ->yes, MAILSFLD should be valid then[1.24]
         TM    MAILFLG2,MFLG2VLF Validate fail for other reason  [1.23]
         BO    BADSFLD      -> yes,  ignore MAILSFLD regardless  [1.24]
RSCSREJ  EQU   *             <-here if if RSCS reject.  Check    [1.24]
*                            validity of MAILSFLD anyhow....     [1.24]
         ICM   R7,B'1111',MAILSFLD   AT LEAST A VALID SENDER FIELD?
         BZ    BADSFLD       SORRY, KILL IT                      [1.24]
         USING FIELDD,R7     ADDRESS THE SENDER FIELDD
         ICM   R7,B'1111',FIPARS  GET MBOX BLOCK POINTER
         BZ    BADSFLD       NEVER PARSED AN ADDRESS             [1.24]
         USING MBOX,R7     ADDRESS THE ADDRESS BLOCK
         ST    R7,MBOXP            Save for later use.
         MVC   STKP,=A(LCLSTACK)   Init stack pointer
         MVC   STKL,=A(L'LCLSTACK)    and length.
         L     R5,MBXLCL         GET USER LIST
         L     R7,MBXDML         GET HOST LIST
         DROP  R7
         ST    R5,NODEP            Set NODE pointer.
         CALL  GENLIST,(NODEP,LSTRA,LSTRL,STKP,STKL) Expand localpart.
         LTR   R15,R15             Did it work?
         BNZ   BADSFLD             No  : Bad sender.
         L     R4,LSTRL            Get localpart length.
         L     R5,LSTRA            Get localpart address.
         ST    R7,NODEP            Set NODE pointer.
         CALL  GENLIST,(NODEP,DSTRA,DSTRL,STKP,STKL) Expand domain.
         LTR   R15,R15             Did it work?
         BNZ   BADSFLD             No  : Bad sender.
         L     R6,DSTRL            Get domain length.
         L     R7,DSTRA            Get domain address.
         B     CHEKLOOP      -> now go check case (3) for loop   [1.24]
         SPACE ,                                                 [1.24]
BADSFLD  EQU   *             <- invalid SFLD comes here          [1.24]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.24]
* (2) MAILSFLD invalid, set up ptrs to MAILUSER and MAILNODE.    [1.24]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.24]
         XC    MBOXP,MBOXP         Clear pointer to bad MBOX.
         LA    R5,MAILUSER   point to userid string              [1.24]
         L     R4,MAILULEN   length of this string               [1.24]
         LA    R7,MAILNODE   point to hostname string            [1.24]
         L     R6,MAILNLEN   length of this string               [1.24]
*  fall thru to CHEKLOOP:                                        [1.24]
CHEKLOOP EQU   *             <- here to do case (3)              [1.24]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.24]
* (3) Check to see if recipient of error mail is a mail server.  [1.24]
* At this point,  registers are as follows:                      [1.24]
*   R5 - userid  R4 - length                                     [1.24]
*   R7 - host    R6 - length                                     [1.24]
*                                                                [1.24]
*  (a) Look up host ROUTD (outgoing, domains tables) to obtain   [1.24]
*      rscs node name for given host's server.                   [1.24]
*  (b) Using host -> rscs node mapping from (a), look in incoming[1.24]
*      table to see if server is there.                          [1.24]
*  If (b)finds a match,  then we can be pretty sure we're        [1.24]
*  trying to send error mail to a server which is a loop.        [1.24]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.24]
* (a) Get ROUTD for given host to obtain RSCS node name.         [1.24]
        CALL  FNROUTD,((R7),(R6)) look up returnee host          [1.22]
        LTR   R8,R15         no such host?                       [1.24]
        BZ    RETKILL        kill it for fun.                    [1.24]
        USING ROUTD,R8       address the routed returned         [1.24]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.24]
* (b) Use above RTROUTE to build key for INCOMING lookup which   [1.24]
*     is a 16 byte string of "node    user    ".  Before looking [1.24]
*     there,  check to make sure user@node isn't self.           [1.24]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.24]
        C     R4,=F'8'       if the userid is >8, not much point [1.24]
        BH    MRET           in continuing the lookup.           [1.24]
        MVC   LOOKNODE,RTROUTE set up lookup stuff for MAILVTAB  [1.24]
        DROP  R8             done w/routd                        [1.24]
        MVC   LOOKUSER,=CL8' ' blank it first                    [1.24]
        LR    R1,R4          get length into r1                  [1.24]
        BCTR  R1,0           decrement for EX                    [1.24]
        EX    R1,MOVELOOK    MVC LOOKUSER,0(R5)                  [1.24]
        CLC   LOOKNODE,CPUSTR is it the local node?              [1.24]
        BNE   SKIPLOC        ->nope,  skip next test             [1.24]
        CLC   LOOKUSER,MAILVMID is it my own VMID?               [1.24]
        BE    NETLOOP        -> that's a loop                    [1.24]
SKIPLOC EQU   *              <- wasn't self                      [1.24]
        L     R8,MAILVTAB    get address of incoming table       [1.24]
        CALL  TBLUK,((R8),LOOKVALD,L'LOOKVALD,TWORK)  look it up [1.24]
        LTR   R15,R15        is it a trusted mailer?             [1.24]
        BNZ   MRET           ->no,  so we may continue           [1.24]
        B     NETLOOP        ->yes,  this would cause a mail loop[1.24]
         B     MRET          DO COMMON RETURN CODE NOW
        SPACE ,                                                  [1.24]
MOVELOOK MVC  LOOKUSER,0(R5) executed MVC                        [1.24]
        SPACE
NETLOOP EQU   *      [1.20]
        WTR   RTS028 [1.20]
* fall thru to retkill... [1.20]
RETKILL  EQU   *
         WTR   RTS037        INVALID FILE FROM ANOTHER MAILER
         B     ERRLOOP       USE THE SAME RETURN TO MAINTAINER
         SPACE ,
*--- COMMON RETURN STUFF ---*
MRET     EQU   *
         WTR   RTS029,(CA,(R5),CA,(R7))
         LA    R1,CPSPOOL
         LA    R0,CPSPLEN
         DC    X'83100008'   PUNCH THIS TO MYSELF
         MVI   CARD,C' '     INIT TO BLANKS
         MVC   CARD+1(79),CARD
         MVC   CARD(6),=C'Date: '
         LA    R1,CARD+6
         L     R15,AARPADAT            [1]
         BALR  R14,R15
         PUNCHC CARD
         MVI   CARD,C' '
         MVC   CARD+1(79),CARD
         MVC   CARD(22),=CL22'From: Network Mailer <' [1.20]
         MVC   CARD+22(8),MAILVMID     MY USERID
         LA    R2,CARD+30    [1.20] point to end of userid
ULOOP    EQU   *             [1.20] loop to trim trailing blanks
         CLI   0(R2),C' '    [1.20] trim of trailing blanks
         BNE   ULOOPOUT      [1.20] out of loop
         BCTR  R2,0          [1.20] decrement
         B     ULOOP         [1.20] loop back
ULOOPOUT EQU   *             [1.20]
         MVI   1(R2),C'@'    [1.20] stuff in the atsign
         MVC   2(8,R2),CPUSTR [1.20] now drag in my host name
         LA    R2,10(R2)     [1.20] point to end of host name
HLOOP    EQU   *             [1.20] same kind of loop to trim...
         CLI   0(R2),C' '    [1.20] blank?
         BNE   HLOOPOUT      [1.20] done
         BCTR  R2,0          [1.20] decr
         B     HLOOP         [1.20] zzzz
HLOOPOUT EQU   *             [1.20]
         MVI   1(R2),C'>'    [1.20] Complete the line
         PUNCHC CARD
         MVI   CARD,C' '
         MVC   CARD+1(79),CARD
         MVC   CARD(25),=C'Subject: Undelivered mail'
         PUNCHC CARD
         MVI   CARD,C' '
         MVC   CARD+1(79),CARD
         MVC   CARD(4),=C'To: '
         LA    R2,CARD+4     DESTINATION OF COPY
         CLC   MBOXP,=A(0)         Is the MBOX pointer valid?
         BE    TOSTR               No  : Use the strings.
         MVC   STKP,=A(LCLSTACK)   Init stack pointer
         MVC   STKL,=A(L'LCLSTACK)    and length.
         CALL  GENMBOX,(MBOXP,TOADDR,TOLEN,STKP,STKL) Expand address.
         L     R1,TOLEN            Get address length.
         BCTR  R1,0
         L     R3,TOADDR           Get address address.
         EX    R1,COPY             "MVC 0(*-*,R2),0(R3)"
         B     TOPUNCH
TOSTR    DS    0H
         LR    R1,R4         LENGTH OF COPY
         BCTR  R1,0          -1 FOR EXECUTE
         LR    R3,R5         SOURCE OF COPY
         EX    R1,COPY       COPY USER NAME IN
         AR    R2,R4         [1.20] POINT PAST USER NAME
         MVI   0(R2),C'@'   [1.20]
         LA    R2,1(R2)      [1.20] point past "@"
         LR    R1,R6         LENGTH OF HOST NAME
         BCTR  R1,0          -1 FOR EXECUTE
         LR    R3,R7         ADDRESS OF NAME
         EX    R1,COPY       COPY IN THE HOST NAME
TOPUNCH  DS    0H
         PUNCHC CARD         PUNCH THE TO: CARD
         MVI   CARD,C' '
         MVC   CARD+1(79),CARD
         PUNCHC CARD         END OF MESSAGE HEADER
         PUNCHC EMSG1        PUNCH THE LITTLE APOLOGY
         PUNCHC EMSG2        PUNCH THE LITTLE APOLOGY
         MVI   CARD,C' '
         MVC   CARD+1(79),CARD
         PUNCHC CARD         PRINT A BLANK LINE FOR READABILITY
         L     R5,MAILULFS   user log fscb                       [1.23]
         FSCLOSE FSCB=(R5),ERROR=DUNFILE                         [1.23]
         FSPOINT FSCB=(R5),RDPNT=1,ERROR=DUNFILE                 [1.23]
FSLOOP   EQU   *
         FSREAD  FSCB=(R5),BUFFER=CARD,BSIZE=80,ERROR=DUNFILE    [1.23]
         PUNCHC CARD
         B     FSLOOP
DUNFILE  EQU   *
         FSCLOSE FSCB=(R5)                                       [1.23]
         FSERASE FSCB=(R5)                                       [1.23]
         MVI   CARD,C' '
         MVC   CARD+1(79),CARD
         PUNCHC CARD
         SPACE ,                                                 [1.22]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.22]
* If SMTP,  send back the SMTP REPLY too.                        [1.22]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.22]
         TM    MAILFLG2,MFLG2SMT  was it SMTP                    [1.22]
         BNO   SKIPSMTP           no sir                         [1.22]
         PUNCHC SMTSEPR           a little seperator message     [1.22]
         PUNCHC CARD              and another blank line         [1.22]
SMTPLOOP EQU   *                                                 [1.22]
         MVI   CARD,C' '          blank it out                   [1.22]
         MVC   CARD+1(79),CARD                                   [1.22]
         FSREAD 'SMTP REPLY',BUFFER=CARD,BSIZE=80,ERROR=SMTPEND, [1.22]*
               FORM=E
         LR    R5,R1              hold on fscb                   [1.22]
         PUNCHC CARD                                             [1.22]
         B     SMTPLOOP           keep on punching               [1.22]
SMTPEND  EQU   *                  done                           [1.22]
         FSCLOSE FSCB=(R5)        close the file                 [1.23]
SKIPSMTP EQU   *                  here if not SMTP               [1.22]
         SPACE ,                                                 [1.22]
         PUNCHC SEPR
         LA    R5,MAILSFB    GET SFBLOK
         USING SFBLOK,R5
         LH    R5,SFBRECSZ   GET RECORD SIZE
         DROP  R5
         SPACE ,
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
*  CHECK TO SEE IF THE HEADER WAS SUCCESFULLY SCANNED.  IF SO, THEN
*  THE PUNHDR, PUNTXT, AND PUNCLS ROUTINES CAN BE USED. IF NO, THEN
*  JUST COPY THE READER FILE (INCLUDING POSSIBLE "INVISIBLE" FIELDS).
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
         TM    MAILFLG1,MFLG1HDS       HEADER SCANNED OK?
         BNO   HDNOSCN       HEADER NOT SCANNED
         L     R15,APUNHDR   GET HEADER PUNCHER
         CALL  (15),((R11))  CALL IT
         L     R15,APUNTXT   GET TEXT PUNCHER
         CALL  (15),((R11))
         L     R15,APUNCLS
         CALL  (15),((R11))
         B     SKIPOVER      SKIP THE NEXT PART
         SPACE ,
HDNOSCN  EQU   *
DECKLOOP EQU   *
         RDCARD CARD,(R5),ERROR=DUNDECK
         PUNCHC CARD
         B     DECKLOOP
DUNDECK  EQU   *
         LA    R1,CPCLOSE
         LA    R0,CPCLLEN
         DC    X'83100008'
SKIPOVER EQU   *
         SR    R15,R15
RET      EQU   *
         L     R13,4(R13)              GET CALLER'S SAVE PTR
         L     R14,12(R13)             GET R14
         LM    R0,R12,20(R13)          GET R0-R12
         BR    R14                     RETURN
         SPACE ,
ERRLOOP  EQU   *             ERROR LOOP DETECTED
         CLC   MAINTNOD,CPUSTR IS MAINTAINER ON THIS MACHINE?
         BNE   ERR2          NOPE
         CLC   MAINTID,MAILVMID DON'T LET MAINTAINER=MAILER!!
         BNE   ERR2          GOOD, THEN I CAN SEND IT TO HIM
         WTR   RTS028        ELSE, ERROR LOOP
         SR    R15,R15
         B     RET
ERR2     EQU   *
         LA    R5,MAINTID    SEND FILE TO MAINTID
         LA    R4,8          LENGTH OF IT
         LA    R7,MAINTNOD   MAINTAINER'S NODE
         LA    R6,8          LENGTH
         B     MRET          ERROR LOOP FIXUP
COPY     MVC   0(0,R2),0(R3)
         LTORG ,
FR       DC    C'From: Network Mailer <         at         >'
EMSG1 DC CL80'Your mail was not delivered to some or all of its'
EMSG2 DC CL80'intended recipients for the following reason(s):'
SEPR     DC    CL80' '
         ORG   SEPR
         DC    20C'-',C'RETURNED MAIL FILE',20C'-'
         ORG
SMTSEPR  DC    CL80'SMTP Transaction log follows:'               [1.22]
CPSPOOL  DC    C'SP PUN TO * CLASS M',X'15'
         DC    C'TAG DEV PUN --- returned mail file ---'
CPSPLEN  EQU   *-CPSPOOL
CPCLOSE  DC    C'SP PUN CLOSE',X'15',C'SP PUN OFF',X'15'
         DC    C'TAG DEV PUN'
CPCLLEN  EQU   *-CPCLOSE
         SPACE ,
SAVE     DS    18F                     SAVE AREA
CARD     DS    CL132
TWORK    DS    64F   [1.20]
LOOKVALD DS    CL16                                              [1.24]
         ORG   LOOKVALD                                          [1.24]
LOOKNODE DS    CL8                                               [1.24]
LOOKUSER DS    CL8                                               [1.24]
         ORG   ,                                                 [1.24]
TOADDR   DS    A                   Address of to-address.
TOLEN    DS    A                   Length of to-address.
LSTRA    DS    A                   Address of localpart.
LSTRL    DS    F                   Length of localpart.
DSTRA    DS    A                   Address of domainpart.
DSTRL    DS    F                   Length of domainpart.
STKP     DS    A                   Stack Pointer.
STKL     DS    F                   Stack Length.
MBOXP    DS    A                   Address of MBOX for addressee.
NODEP    DS    A                   Address of NODE for GENLIST.
LCLSTACK DS    XL100               Local stack area.
         END   MAILRET
